1
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:09,260
A town had 8,000 people.

2
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:15,150
10 years later, its population is 150 per cent of what it was.

3
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,660
How many people live in the town now?

4
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:21,230
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:25,760
100 per cent is the whole amount: 8,000 people.

6
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,670
50 per cent is half of that: 4,000.

7
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:33,490
150 per cent is 8,000 plus 4,000.

8
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:37,620
The town now has 12,000 people.

9
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:41,420
Remember: to find 10 per cent, divide by 10.

10
00:00:41,470 --> 00:00:44,900
To find 1 per cent, divide by 100.

11
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:48,740
You can build other percentages from these.

12
00:00:48,790 --> 00:00:55,360
10 per cent of 320 is 32, so 30 per cent is 3 times 32, which is 96.

13
00:00:55,410 --> 00:00:58,080
100 per cent is the whole amount.

14
00:00:58,130 --> 00:01:02,670
More than 100 per cent means more than the whole.

15
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:05,250
150 per cent is 1.5 as a decimal.

16
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:09,010
It means one and a half times the amount.

17
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:12,520
200 per cent is 2: double the amount.

18
00:01:12,570 --> 00:01:15,340
And 250 per cent is 2.5.

19
00:01:15,390 --> 00:01:21,950
The rule is the same as before: to change a percentage to a decimal, divide by 100.

20
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:22,710
Your turn.

21
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:25,150
Write 175 per cent as a decimal.

22
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:28,620
Pause the video and try it.

23
00:01:28,670 --> 00:01:31,200
175 divided by 100 is 1.75.

24
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:35,400
The digits move 2 places to the right.

25
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:37,930
A percentage can also be very small.

26
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:41,870
Less than 1 per cent is less than one hundredth.

27
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:45,200
0.5 per cent is half of 1 per cent.

28
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:49,760
As a decimal, 0.5 divided by 100 is 0.005.

29
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:54,170
A bank pays 0.5 per cent interest on 600 dollars.

30
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:59,490
1 per cent of 600 is 6, so 0.5 per cent is 3 dollars.

31
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:00,350
Your turn.

32
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,670
Find 0.1 per cent of 3,000.

33
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:06,390
Pause the video and try it.

34
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:08,730
1 per cent of 3,000 is 30.

35
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:13,410
0.1 per cent is one tenth of that, which is 3.

36
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:14,880
Here is the method.

37
00:02:14,930 --> 00:02:19,210
Step 1: change the percentage to a decimal and multiply.

38
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:24,240
Or build it from 100 per cent, 10 per cent and 1 per cent.

39
00:02:24,290 --> 00:02:30,290
Step 2: more than 100 per cent gives an answer bigger than the amount.

40
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:36,940
Step 3: less than 1 per cent gives an answer smaller than one hundredth of the amount.

41
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:41,380
Step 4: check that the size of your answer makes sense.

42
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:44,540
Find 145 per cent of 80.

43
00:02:44,590 --> 00:02:46,270
100 per cent is 80.

44
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:49,830
10 per cent is 8, so 40 per cent is 32.

45
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:54,940
And 5 per cent is half of 10 per cent, which is 4.

46
00:02:54,990 --> 00:02:59,320
Add them: 80 plus 32 plus 4 is 116.

47
00:02:59,370 --> 00:03:00,620
Check the size.

48
00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:05,860
145 per cent is more than the whole, and 116 is more than 80.

49
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:06,840
Good.

50
00:03:06,890 --> 00:03:10,300
Find 0.4 per cent of 2,500.

51
00:03:10,350 --> 00:03:11,800
1 per cent is 25.

52
00:03:11,850 --> 00:03:15,790
0.1 per cent is one tenth of that: 2.5.

53
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:20,320
0.4 per cent is 4 times 2.5, which is 10.

54
00:03:20,370 --> 00:03:24,650
Write 3.6 per cent as a decimal, and as a fraction.

55
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:26,660
First, the decimal.

56
00:03:26,710 --> 00:03:30,170
3.6 divided by 100 is 0.036.

57
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:32,420
0.036 is 36 thousandths.

58
00:03:32,470 --> 00:03:35,700
Divide the top and the bottom by 4.

59
00:03:35,750 --> 00:03:38,030
That is 9 over 250.

60
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:40,460
A kitten weighed 0.8 kilograms.

61
00:03:40,510 --> 00:03:43,210
Now it weighs 350 per cent of that.

62
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:45,570
What does it weigh now?

63
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:49,170
350 per cent is 3.5 as a decimal.

64
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:51,130
3.5 times 0.8 is 2.8.

65
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:55,050
The kitten now weighs 2.8 kilograms.

66
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:57,070
Find 0.3 per cent of 700.

67
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,850
Here is Raj's working.

68
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:01,670
Which line goes wrong first?

69
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:03,220
Line 1 is wrong.

70
00:04:03,270 --> 00:04:08,060
0.3 per cent means 0.3 out of 100, which is 0.003.

71
00:04:08,110 --> 00:04:12,300
An answer of 210 would be 30 per cent.

72
00:04:12,350 --> 00:04:14,400
0.003 times 700 is 2.1.

73
00:04:14,450 --> 00:04:19,700
That is a sensible size for such a small percentage.

74
00:04:19,750 --> 00:04:22,190
Big percentages describe growth.

75
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:28,010
The population of India today is about 400 per cent of what it was in 1950.

76
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:31,440
That is about 4 times as many people.

77
00:04:31,490 --> 00:04:33,610
Small percentages matter too.

78
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:38,200
Carbon dioxide is only about 0.04 per cent of the air.

79
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:40,800
That is 4 parts in every 10,000.

80
00:04:40,850 --> 00:04:45,960
But even that small amount helps to keep our planet warm.

81
00:04:46,010 --> 00:04:47,390
One last question.

82
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:49,610
What is 200 per cent of 7.5?

83
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:53,150
Pause the video and answer.

84
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:55,860
200 per cent means double.

85
00:04:55,910 --> 00:04:58,290
2 times 7.5 is 15.

86
00:04:58,340 --> 00:05:04,240
To remember: to change any percentage to a decimal, divide by 100.

87
00:05:04,290 --> 00:05:09,030
150 per cent is 1.5, and 0.5 per cent is 0.005.

88
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:13,150
Over 100 per cent gives more than the amount.

89
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:17,480
Under 1 per cent gives less than one hundredth of it.

90
00:05:17,530 --> 00:05:25,700
Build percentages from 100 per cent, 10 per cent and 1 per cent, and check the size of your answer.

91
00:05:25,750 --> 00:05:31,150
Great work! Now practise lesson 10.2 on Camday.
